    {
      "ad_archive_id": "1640641344082391",
      "collation_count": 1,
      "collation_id": "1574947153960566",
      "is_active": true,
      "page_id": "696068746913122",
      "page_is_deleted": false,
      "snapshot": {
        "branded_content": null,
        "page_id": "696068746913122",
        "page_is_deleted": false,
        "page_profile_uri": "https://www.instagram.com/_u/granburydc",
        "root_reshared_post": null,
        "byline": null,
        "disclaimer_label": null,
        "page_name": "granburydc",
        "page_profile_picture_url": "https://scontent-phl2-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-19/590411771_17917474281211049_7311950782158061825_n.jpg?REDACTED",
        "event": null,
        "caption": null,
        "cta_text": null,
        "cards": [],
        "body": {
          "text": "If you’re afraid of the dentist, you might feel a little silly about it. Like it’s an overreaction, or something you should have outgrown by now.\n\nDr. Buske wants you to know it’s none of those things.\n\nIn his experience, dental fear is almost never about the dentist at all. It usually traces back to one specific memory, something that happened years ago, maybe in childhood. A painful visit. A moment you felt out of control. Something that stuck.\n\nAnd that memory doesn’t simply stay in the past. It gets triggered the second you lean back in the chair. Your body remembers before your mind can catch up, and the fear comes rushing in, even when you logically know you’re safe.\n\nHere’s why that understanding matters. When we care for an anxious patient, we’re not only treating teeth. We’re working around that memory too, going slower, explaining more, and giving you back the sense of control that old moment took away.\n\nYour fear isn’t irrational. It makes complete sense. And you deserve a team that treats the whole of it, not only the tooth.\n\nIf fear has kept you from the care you need, let us meet you where you are. Come see us at Granbury Dental Center in Granbury, TX.\n\n📞 Call: (817) 573-3761\n🌐 Visit granburydentalcenter.com or tap the link in our bio to learn more\n\n#GranburyTX #GranburyDentist #DentalAnxiety #GentleDentistry #GranburyDentalCenter"
        },
        "cta_type": null,
        "display_format": "VIDEO",
        "link_description": null,
        "link_url": null,
        "images": [],
        "page_categories": [
          "Profile"
        ],
        "page_like_count": 0,
        "title": null,
